The reason there is a `KeyError` is because the graph is trying to look for the next node to run, which in my case is named `MongoDBAgent`. But, if you take a look at the logs, it's trying to run "MongoMongoDBMongoDBAgent" which doesn't make sense.

This is most definitely because my `AgentState` looks like this:

```python
class AgentState(TypedDict):
    """
    The agent state is the input to each node in the graph
    """

    messages: Annotated[Sequence[BaseMessage], operator.add]
    """
    The annotation tells the graph that new messages will always be added
    to the current state
    """

    next: str
    """
    The next node to execute
    """
```

~~The culprit, I think is the `operator.add` in the Annotated messages.~~ I did see a [similar issue](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/issues/78#issuecomment-1927513557) that I will be diving into.

@jackiezhangcn this is happening because you have a python file called `langgraph.py` in your current working directory.

Python imports modules with precedence of local file -> installed package in PATH, etc.

If you change your file name to something different, it will work.

