For anyone having this issue. Turned out the root case (in our case) was the mismatch between the "tool" decorator from langchain which have the "input" schema in Pydantic model and the actual function definition with "default" paramterer settings.

Here sample:

```python
class SearchInput(BaseModel):
    search_query: str = Field(description="should be a search query")
    top_k: int = Field(description="should be a number")
    language: str = Field(description="the product documentation language", default="all")

@tool("documentation", args_schema=SearchInput)
def documentation(search_query: str, top_k: int, language: str = "all") -> MutableSequence[Document]:
   .....
```

When the Model JSON response is enabled, then request can't have "default" values ... so removing from the function definition `= "all"`, then it will complain. Changing to this .. make it throw:

