```

@minki-j the update from `last_node` is in fact applied to the state of the Level 1 graph, but since Level 1 graph is invoked inside the Level 0 graph, Level 1 graph as a whole **still** needs to respect the state of the parent (Level 0) graph. if you want to keep the state schemas independent, i.e. have no overlapping keys, you can just add input/output transformations before/after you invoke level 1 graph

see more here: https://langchain-ai.github.io/langgraph/concepts/low_level/#as-a-function

