I am running into same issue and was able to pinpoint what was the error , at least in our case. For some reason, the next message sent my user created a new branch. To get the messages, frontend SDK starts a BFS search from the history and looks for a state with no parent i.e. `state.parent_checkpoint == null`. 

However, because it becomes a branch off, the parent checkpoint is not null and it leads to not parsing any messages. This code is written in `stream.js` in method `getBranchSequence`.

