- block returns a terminal tool message and never calls the tool;
- modify executes only the effective args and records both original and effective digests;
- approved but not attempted is distinguishable from blocked;
- execution failure is distinguishable from policy denial;
- retry with the same proposed_call_id preserves the decision_id;
- retry with changed args requires a new decision;
- partial completion records a result state without pretending success.

That keeps the hook useful now without forcing a full receipt system into the first API. The important part is reserving the join points so a later audit or receipt layer can prove which decision authorized which execution result.

