@nick-hollon-lc — sorry to tag directly; flagging this since it's a self-contained pregel-runner perf fix and I'd love to get it (and its sibling #8220) unblocked if the approach looks right.

The core is a deterministic quadratic in `FuturesDict.on_done`: it re-scans the entire `done` set on every task completion, so a superstep of T parallel tasks does 1+2+…+T = O(T²) lock-guarded `future.exception()`/`cancelled()` calls — profiling a 400-task fan-out showed ~80,000 `future.exception()` calls per invoke, exactly T²/2. The fix is one line (check only the just-completed future — each future passes through `on_done` exactly once, the early-wake still fires at the first failure, and the authoritative stop decision stays in `tick`/`_panic_or_proceed`), taking it to O(T). Full sync+async in-memory pregel suite passes, including the cancellation/interrupt/max-concurrency tests that exercise this path.

Patch is ready on a branch — happy to open the PR through the issue-link gate if you can assign me, or to adjust the approach if you'd prefer a different shape. (#8220 is the same kind of loop-invariant-scan removal in `put_writes`.)
